# Cloudflare Pages reads this file.
#
# Note what it can and can't do. The Cache-Control below reaches the HTML, and
# that is all it reaches: Pages serves static assets with its own four-hour
# caching and ignores what's asked for here. Setting /*.js and /*.css made no
# difference at all - checked live, game.js still came back max-age=14400.
#
# That gap is what broke the K-map button. The browser revalidated the page,
# got the new HTML with the button in it, and paired it with yesterday's
# game.js, which had never heard of the button. It drew, nothing was wired to
# it, and pressing it did nothing at all.
#
# So freshness is the job of the ?v= on every script and stylesheet tag, not of
# this file. Changing it changes their URLs, which no cache can second-guess.
# Run `python3 bump.py` after changing any JS or CSS - see that script.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# These only change when their names do, so they can be kept properly.
/thumbs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/logo.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
